# Build output of the example crates. They are outside the workspace (each has
# its own empty `[workspace]` table), so the repository's own `/target` rule —
# anchored at the root — does not reach them.
target/

# **The two C probes write ELF, and `out/` is not `target/`.** `libgreet` and
# `greeter` are built by their own `build.sh` with the cross toolchain, not by
# cargo, and they put the result in `out/` — which nothing here covered, so a
# 6 KB aarch64 executable and a 5.7 KB shared object were TRACKED. The audit of
# 2026-09-03 found them (its LOW list).
#
# They are build products by every test this repository uses on the question:
# reproducible from `tools/container/exec.sh examples/probes/libgreet/build.sh`
# and then `.../greeter/build.sh`, and named nowhere except by those two scripts
# — `SPEC-02`'s and `rivet-core`'s references to `libgreet.so.1` are the STRING,
# not the file. `examples/README.md` already records what a 9.2 MB tracked
# binary cost when Aura's packaging left; these are the same thing three orders
# of magnitude smaller and no more correct for it.
/probes/greeter/out/
/probes/libgreet/out/

# The Go example's built binary. **Anchored to the file**, because a bare
# `template-go-service` also matches the DIRECTORY of the same name and would
# exclude the whole example from the repository — which it did, silently, on
# 2026-09-01 until `git status` was read rather than assumed.
/templates/template-go-service/template-go-service

# Aura's Go producer, the same trap a second time: `aura-vitals-go` is the name
# of the BINARY and of the DIRECTORY it lives in, so a bare entry would exclude
# the whole example. Anchored to the file, and `git status` read afterwards
# rather than assumed — which is what caught it in September.
/aura/aura-vitals-go/aura-vitals-go

# The stripped cross-built `ble-listen` probe, staged beside its manifest so
# `cargo rivet package --binary` can reach it from Windows — `deploy/launcher`
# in the root ignore file, same reason. Anchored to the FILE, because the
# directory carries the same name and a bare entry would exclude the source
# too, which is the trap the entry above records.
/probes/ble-listen/ble-listen
